# Kedom Foundry system

Architecture decisions and their evidence are in `docs/research/05-decisions.md`. Data shapes are in `docs/system/data-model.md`. Do not re-litigate these in code.

## Hard rules

- **Foundry v14 only.** `minimum: "14.367"`. Never add a v13 compatibility path.
- **ApplicationV2 only.** ApplicationV1 is deprecated until v16. Lancer and StarWarsFFG are stranded on v13 because they never migrated — do not repeat it.
- **Handlebars only. No Svelte, no UI framework inside Foundry.** Tidy 5e's looks are 16,213 lines of plain CSS and 6 lines of scoped Svelte CSS; the framework buys reactivity we do not need. Svelte belongs in `packages/forge/web` only.
- **DataModels only.** `foundry.abstract.TypeDataModel` on `CONFIG.*.dataModels`. `template.json` was removed in v14; never create one.
- **Pure functions** for derivations, action pipelines, and calculated displays (`src/derivations/`, collectors, display helpers): data in, data out. No `game`, no document reads, no I/O, no `await` in pure helpers. `prepareDerivedData` runs on every actor update.
- **Zero-initialise every derived path in `prepareBaseData`.** Active Effects target these paths, and an absent path fails silently depending on preparation order.
- **Keys are identity; display labels are not.** Never parse a name to recover meaning. CoC7, WFRP4e, and SWFFG all do, and renaming silently breaks references. Forge may still store the column as `slug` — same concept (ADR-007).
- **Modifiers retain source.** Every collected modifier carries `{ id, label }` (and optional uuid) so chat can show where a bonus came from (ADR-006).
- **Every user-facing string is localised.** `game.i18n.localize` or the Handlebars `localize` helper; hard-coded English in a template is a bug. UI strings live in `lang/{en,ru}.json`. Content translations live in SQLite and ship as Babele JSON; do not put race descriptions in `lang/ru.json` and do not require Babele. See `docs/forge/localisation.md`.
- **Renaming a derived path is a migration.** Effects in user worlds target them; that path list is public API.

## Do not build

- A rules engine. Modifiers come from independent collector functions returning `Modifier[]`; adding a rule means adding one file. No RuleElement hierarchy (pf2e has 38), no roll-option predicate graph, no Activities (dnd5e's mixin is ~1,400 lines).
- Outcome banding as a blocking dependency. Collect values and sourced modifiers first; map totals to the success ladder when ADR-008 is un-deferred. Skill critical success is gone (three outcomes only).
- User-authored JavaScript in content. Effects are declarative documents plus a named handler registry. WFRP4e ships ~2,100 hashed `.js` files; never that.
- Playwright e2e as a required gate. Unit-test pure logic (ADR-014).
- Extra document types. Two actor types, seven item types. Prefer a `subType` discriminator over a near-identical new type, as WWN did for `power`.

## Conventions

- Sheets declare `static TABS` and `static PARTS`; enrich per tab in `_preparePartContext`. Base class is `KedomDocumentSheet`, in the shape of draw-steel's `DSDocumentSheet`.
- `data-action` dispatch, not per-element listeners.
- Preserve scroll and focus across re-renders in the base sheet class.
- Numbered migrations in `src/migrations/NNN-description.ts`, one class each. Never a monolith.
- Dice expressions and thresholds come from `src/config/`, never hard-coded — defaults are settled in `docs/rules/20-skills.md` (`2d10` skills/saves, `d20` attacks).
- Typed ChatMessage DataModels persist the labelled, **sourced** modifier list, so cards explain themselves and stay interactive.
- All user-facing strings go through `lang/{en,ru}.json`. No literals in templates or code.
- Full CSS cascade-layer / “slick” budget is deferred (ADR-013).

## Budget

Under 10,000 lines of logic for v1. dnd5e is ~100k and pf2e ~124k because of scope, not polish. If a change needs a new abstraction layer, say so rather than adding it quietly.
